  "hostname": "BL-LT-0107",
  "reason": "KB-014 quick check: confirm whether laptop has a path to the internet"
}

{
  "outcome": "needs_user_info",
  "reply_to_user": "Hi Sofia, sorry you're stuck without internet today. Our records show your laptop hasn't been able to reach our systems, which fits what you're seeing. Please try these steps in order and check after each one whether websites load:\n1. Check whether other devices on your home Wi-Fi, like your phone or TV, can get online. If none of them can, the problem is your home internet, not your laptop.\n2. Turn your laptop's Wi-Fi off and back on. If that doesn't help, forget your home network and reconnect to it.\n3. Restart your laptop.\n4. Restart your home router: unplug it, wait about 30 seconds, plug it back in and give it a few minutes to come back up.\n5. If it still doesn't work, connect to your phone's hotspot or plug in a network cable. That tells us whether the laptop itself is working.\nOnce you're back online, please leave the laptop on and signed in for about 30 minutes. It hasn't checked in with us for about 12 days, and that gives it time to pick up any updates it has missed.\nPlease reply and tell us whether your other devices work and which of these steps, if any, fixed it. If nothing works, even on the hotspot, let us know and we'll pass it on for more help.",
  "internal_note": "User: Sofia Rossi (id 7). Account is active, VPN access is enabled, no lockout or sign-in block. Working from home. Device BL-LT-0107 shows offline, last check-in 2026-09-29, with the warning 'No check-in for 12 days'. Per KB-014, offline status confirms the laptop has no path to the internet. Sent the user the KB-014 home fix steps (Wi-Fi toggle, forget network, restart laptop, restart router, hotspot/wired test) and asked whether other devices on her network work. Per KB-018, the check-in gap is over 7 days and needs follow-up: asked the user to stay online and signed in for 30 min once connected. Next steps: re-run check_device_status after the user reports back to confirm a fresh check-in. Escalate to Tier 2 if the laptop fails on a hotspot or wired connection too (possible network adapter or OS problem), or if it comes online but still doesn't check in after a restart (KB-018). Not an office outage, so P1/P2 escalation doesn't apply.",
  "kb_articles": [
    "KB-014",
    "KB-018"
  ],
  "confidence": "medium"
}
